From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rowley <johnrowleyster@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:28:17 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(miniwin): draw immediate mode, viewport rectangles and
 rectangle clears on OpenGL ES 3

Implement SubmitImmediate, SetViewportRect and ClearRect on the OpenGL ES 3
backend, with the software backend and the SDL GPU backend as the
reference, and report it in Miniwin_DeviceDrawsImmediateMode.

- Transform, back-face culling, Direct3D lighting and vertex fog run on
  the CPU through immediatemode.cpp, as on the other backends. A second
  program takes the clip-space vertices and applies texture stage 0
  (point or bilinear through texelFetch, colour-keyed texels discarded),
  the specular colour and vertex or table fog. Colours are interpolated
  linearly on screen (GLSL ES 3.00 has no noperspective, so they travel
  multiplied by w); texture coordinates are perspective-correct. Vertices
  are shifted half a pixel to sample where Direct3D's rasterizer does.
- The depth buffer holds Direct3D's z / w for immediate mode, so the
  depth comparisons map directly and a rectangle clear stores z as given.
  Rectangle clears are scissored glClears.
- Draws happen at once. Retained mode gets its program, states and
  viewport back before its next mesh after an immediate-mode draw, a
  clear or a 2D image.
- Viewport rectangles project and clip retained and immediate-mode draws.
  Viewport rectangles, rectangle clears and 2D images are clipped to the
  virtual display's fit, so the bars stay black.
- Textures are keyed (colour key and decal colour) as the software
  backend keys them, for both modes.
- The picture follows the resizable window: Flip scales the target to the
  window's current size, nearest-neighbour at a whole multiple and
  bilinear otherwise, resolving a multisampled target first; 2D images
  at a scale that is not whole are filtered with their edge texels
  mapped to their edge pixels, as on SDL GPU; Download reads the fit
  (MINIWIN_DUMP_FRAME). The renderer's own ViewportTransform, which hid
  the base class's and left GetFitRect and GetViewportTransform unset, is
  gone.
- Listing: before SetCooperativeLevel gives miniwin its window, the
  device is tried on a hidden OpenGL window of its own when the client's
  windows are OpenGL windows (Miniwin_SetOpenGLWindows), and not listed
  otherwise. SDL GPU is not listed for an OpenGL window on any platform:
  on Wayland its claim is a protocol error that closes the display
  connection, as Vulkan finds the window in use on Android.
- The 'Unsupported number of lights' error is logged once: immediate mode
  lights with every light.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

